.TH geectl-pull-request-comment 1  "geectl-pull-request-comment 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-pull\-request\-comment \- Comment on a pull request. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl pull\-request comment\fR [\fB\-\-parent\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-body\fR> <\fIREFERENCE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Comment on a pull request. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-body\fR \fI<BODY>\fR
The comment text. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: the body may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-parent\fR \fI<PARENT>\fR
The comment being replied to, when this is a reply (OBS only; refused on a Gitea ref)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREFERENCE\fR>
The pull\-request handle: `obs:<id>` or `gitea:<owner>/<repo>#<number>`
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
